'''''Sorbus maderensis''''' is a species of [[rowan]] in the family [[Rosaceae]] that is [[endemic]] to [[Madeira]].  It is threatened by [[habitat loss]].

==Etymology==
''Sorbus'' is the [[Latin]] name for the fruit of the service tree. ''Maderensis'' means 'from [[Madeira]]'.<ref name="gledhill">Gledhill, David (2008). "The Names of Plants". Cambridge University Press. {{ISBN|9780521866453}} (hardback), {{ISBN|9780521685535}} (paperback).  pp 247, 356</ref>

